\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $e$ | $8$ | $4$ |\n| $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $e+4$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row), and we compute \n$Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\  & =4\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4) \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4) \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $e$ | $8$ | $4$ |\n| $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $e+4$ | $10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)$ | $5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)$ |" 13194139539466 17592186576411 true] [17592186357382 1074 "To get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =e+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $e$ | $8$ | $4$ |\n| $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $e+4$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row), and we compute \n$Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\  & =4\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4) \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4) \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =10\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $e$ | $8$ | $4$ |\n| $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $e+4$ | $10\\operatorname{ln